      "summary_source": "But scientists say the world could get back to 1.5C through deep, rapid emissions cuts and removing carbon from the atmosphere Global heating will reach at least 1.8C under even the most optimistic future, well beyond the Paris agreement goal of 1.5C, according to a UN report that warns every fraction of temperature rise intensifies destructive extreme weather, glacier melt, ecosystem loss, and island and coastal city submersion. The report by the Nairobi-based UN Environment Programme confirmed overshooting the 1.5C goal inscribed in the landmark Paris agreement of 2015 was now “unavoidable” and, despite some progress in addressing the human-caused climate crisis driven by burning fossil fuels, likely in the next few years. Continue reading...",
      "summary_zh": "联合国环境规划署发布报告称，即使在最乐观的情景下，全球变暖也将达到至少 1.8 摄氏度，突破《巴黎协定》确定的 1.5 摄氏度目标已不可避免。温度上升将加剧极端天气、冰川融化与生态系统损失。科学家指出，唯有通过深度、快速减排并从大气中清除碳，才有望在未来使气温回落至 1.5 摄氏度。",
