      "title_zh": "墨西哥与巴西的石油协议引发对生态系统和能源转型的担忧",
      "summary_source": "- This June, Pemex and Petrobras, the state fossil fuel companies of Mexico and Brazil respectively, announced a two-year partnership to jointly explore mature and deepwater oilfields in the Gulf of Mexico. - Details of the exact arrangement have not been released, despite both companies being state-run and campaigners’ calls for greater transparency, but subsequent reports suggest that exploration could focus on the Bay of Campeche, near the Gulf’s largest marine protected area and several vulnerable reef habitats. - Both companies have downplayed the significance of the deal as a preliminary step, but environmental campaigners said it risks tying both nations to decades of fossil fuel emissions and pollution. - Supporters hope the partnership will help staunch a recent run of safety incidents at Mexican petrochemical sites.",
      "summary_zh": "巴西国家石油公司与墨西哥国家石油公司于今年 6 月宣布建立为期两年的合作伙伴关系，计划在墨西哥湾共同开发成熟油田和深水油田。环保人士与研究人员对此表示担忧，认为缺乏透明度的协议可能导致两国陷入长达数十年的化石燃料排放，并增加墨西哥湾海洋生态系统的污染与生态风险。",
      "theme_zh": "化石燃料与能源转型",
      "why_zh": "该国企合作引发了拉美国家在追求能源主权与长期气候转型目标之间的政策张力，环保组织对潜在的生态破坏与长期碳锁定时限提出了严重关切（基于事实）。",
